[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]

; The ground: the imported driveway, placed. src/world/ground.gd has the whole
; argument — what the model is, why this scene exists at all, and why nothing out
; here has a collider. What is written down here is the arithmetic that turns the
; model's own metres into the room's floor, because that is what a scene file is
; for and because every number in it is a measurement of the glb beside it rather
; than a taste.
;
; It is named "Ground" and not "Driveway" for the same reason mesh_car.tscn is
; named "Car": the room instances one of these under that name and types it as a
; Ground, and the model is the whole of the outdoors — the concrete, the lawn it
; is let into and the banks that rise away from it — not just the bit the car
; stands on.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/world/ground.gd" id="1_ground"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/models/driveway/sunken_driveway_parking_spot.glb" id="2_model"]

[node name="Ground" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_ground")
concrete = NodePath("Model/Sketchfab_model/Driveway_obj_cleaner_materialmerger_gles/Object_4")

; The one transform in the room that is not a design decision. Every number in it
; is measured off the model, and the model's own frame is the reason each is
; needed:
;
;   SCALE 1.25 — the camera's, not the artist's. The showcase circuit sweeps a
;   5.6 m disc and the model at 1:1 reaches 5.04 m either side of its concrete.
;   A quarter over stands the outer edge 6.30 m out and puts the walk's standoff
;   on the pad rather than over the kerb. ground.gd argues it at length, and
;   tests/integration/test_ground.gd does the sum against Garage's own radius.
;
;   Y -0.15875 — the drivable face of the concrete is 0.1270 m up the model's
;   own axis, and 0.1270 x 1.25 is 0.15875. This is the line that lays the pad a
;   car parks on onto the room's own origin plane, so that the heights authored
;   in garage.gd — eye_position, eye_height_min, eye_height_max — go on meaning
;   heights over the floor a person would be standing on rather than over a
;   plane that happens to pass through the scenery.
;
;   This number used to be -0.504, off a model-space 0.4032, and that was
;   measured off the wrong face (#167). The concrete is not a slab: it is a
;   sunken pad with kerb walls standing up either side of it, and 0.4032 is the
;   top of the kerb. Placing by it put the room's origin plane on the kerb, and
;   because the room then parked every car on ground.gd's drive() — the box
;   round the whole mesh, whose top is that same kerb — all ten cars in the pack
;   stood 34.5 cm above the concrete they looked parked on. The kerb has not
;   moved relative to the pad and drive().end.y still reports it truthfully, at
;   +0.3453 now. What changed is which of the mesh's two faces this file calls
;   the floor, and that the room asks ground.gd's settle() for the surface under
;   the car instead of for the lid of the box.
;
;   The four decimals are a measurement and not a rounding. #167 estimated the
;   drivable face at 0.1272 from the outside; sampled through settle() over the
;   middle of the pad it is 0.1270 flat, and 0.1272 would leave the tyres a
;   quarter of a millimetre under the concrete — inside what a player could see
;   and outside the 0.0001 the suite asserts to.
;
;   X -0.156 and Z -0.309 — the pad's footprint is centred on (0.125, -0.247) in
;   the model rather than on its origin, so without these the car would be parked
;   a hand's width off the middle of its own drive. Same quarter applied: 0.125 x
;   1.25 = 0.156, and 0.247 x 1.25 = 0.309. The sign on Z is the importer's
;   doing — the glb is authored Z-up and comes in turned, which sends the model's
;   +Y down the room's -Z.
;
; What is deliberately NOT here: any import setting. The .import sidecars beside
; the glb are Godot's defaults, and two of those defaults are load-bearing.
;
; No collision is generated, because generating it is something a glTF node asks
; for with a -col suffix and nothing in this model is named that way. That is the
; promise the trees this replaced were held to as well, and it is worth knowing
; it is a default rather than a box somebody remembered to untick — see ground.gd
; on the two rays it would otherwise answer.
;
; The two textures are extracted beside the glb rather than left embedded in it —
; sunken_driveway_parking_spot_0.jpg is the albedo and _1.png the normal map —
; and imported lossless with mipmaps and detect_3d, which is byte for byte the
; same set of parameters the ten cars' maps in assets/models/cars/ already carry.
; #114 asked for a texture convention to be set deliberately the first time
; textures arrived. They arrived with the car pack; this is that convention, and
; the way it is kept is by not overriding it here.
[node name="Model" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_model")]
transform = Transform3D(1.25, 0, 0, 0, 1.25, 0, 0, 0, 1.25, -0.156, -0.15875, -0.309)
